          "description": "Defines a custom resolver.

A resolver can be useful for e.g. locating third-party dependencies.

Returning \`null\` defers to other \`resolveId\` hooks and eventually the default resolution behavior.
Returning \`false\` signals that \`source\` should be treated as an external module and not included in the bundle. If this happens for a relative import, the id will be renormalized the same way as when the {@linkcode InputOptions.external} option is used.
If you return an object, then it is possible to resolve an import to a different id while excluding it from the bundle at the same time.

Note that while \`resolveId\` will be called for each import of a module and can therefore
resolve to the same \`id\` many times, values for \`external\`, \`meta\` or \`moduleSideEffects\`
can only be set once before the module is loaded. The reason is that after this call,
Rolldown will continue with the {@linkcode load} and {@linkcode transform} hooks for that
module that may override these values and should take precedence if they do so.",
        },
        "transform": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {},
              "type": "object",
            },
            {
              "allOf": [
                {
                  "properties": {},
                  "type": "object",
                },
                {
                  "properties": {
                    "order": {
                      "anyOf": [
                        {
                          "anyOf": [
                            {
                              "const": "pre",
                              "type": "string",
                            },
                            {
                              "const": "post",
                              "type": "string",
                            },
                          ],
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "null",
                        },
                      ],
                    },
                  },
                  "type": "object",
                },
                {
                  "properties": {
                    "filter": {
                      "anyOf": [
                        {
                          "additionalProperties": false,
                          "properties": {
                            "code": {
                              "$ref": "#/$defs/GeneralHookFilter",
                              "description": "A filter based on the module's code.

Only available for {@linkcode Plugin.transformtransform} hook.",
                            },
                            "id": {
                              "$ref": "#/$defs/GeneralHookFilter",
                              "description": "A filter based on the module \`id\`.

If the value is a string, it is treated as a glob pattern.
The string type is not available for {@linkcode Plugin.resolveIdresolveId} hook.

If the value is a regular expression, it is tested after the \`id\`'s path separators are normalized to forward slashes (\`/\`).
This keeps the filter portable across operating systems without requiring the regular expression to match both \`/\` and \`\\\`.",
                            },
                            "moduleType": {
                              "anyOf": [
                                {
                                  "items": {
                                    "$ref": "#/$defs/ModuleType_2",
                                  },
                                  "type": "array",
                                },
                                {
                                  "additionalProperties": false,
                                  "properties": {
                                    "include": {
                                      "items": {
                                        "$ref": "#/$defs/ModuleType_2",
                                      },
                                      "type": "array",
                                    },
                                  },
                                  "type": "object",
                                },
                              ],
                              "description": "A filter based on the module's \`moduleType\`.

Only available for {@linkcode Plugin.transformtransform} hook.",
                            },
                          },
                          "type": "object",
                        },
                        {
                          "items": {
                            "$ref": "#/$defs/TopLevelFilterExpression",
                          },
                          "type": "array",
                        },
                      ],
                    },
                  },
                  "type": "object",
                },
              ],
            },
          ],
          "description": "Can be used to transform individual modules.

Note that it's possible to return only properties and no code transformations.

You can use {@linkcode PluginContext.getModuleInfothis.getModuleInfo()} to find out the previous values of \`meta\`, \`moduleSideEffects\` inside this hook.",
        },
        "version": {
          "description": "The version of the plugin, for use in inter-plugin communication scenarios.",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "watchChange": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {},
              "type": "object",
            },
            {
              "allOf": [
                {
                  "properties": {},
                  "type": "object",
                },
                {
                  "properties": {
                    "order": {
                      "anyOf": [
                        {
                          "anyOf": [
                            {
                              "const": "pre",
                              "type": "string",
                            },
                            {
                              "const": "post",
                              "type": "string",
                            },
                          ],
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "null",
                        },
                      ],
                    },
                  },
                  "type": "object",
                },
                {
                  "properties": {
                    "sequential": {
                      "deprecated": true,
                      "type": "boolean",
                    },
                  },
                  "type": "object",
                },
              ],
            },
          ],
          "description": "Notifies a plugin whenever Rolldown has detected a change to a monitored file in watch mode.

If a build is currently running, this hook is called once the build finished.
It will be called once for every file that changed.

This hook cannot be used by output plugins.

If you need to be notified immediately when a file changed, you can use the {@linkcode WatcherOptions.onInvalidatewatch.onInvalidate} option.",
        },
        "writeBundle": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/ObjectHook_8",
          "description": "Called only at the end of {@linkcode RolldownBuild.writebundle.write()} once
all files have been written.",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "api",
        "name",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "PluginMeta": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "description": {
          "description": "A short, human-readable description of what the plugin does.",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "packageName": {
          "description": "The name of the npm package the plugin ships in, e.g. \`@vitejs/plugin-vue\`.",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "version": {
          "description": "The version of the npm package the plugin ships in, e.g. \`5.0.0\`. The
\`version\` field of that package's \`package.json\`.",
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "type": "object",
    },
    "Promise": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {},
      "type": "object",
    },
    "Promise_2": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {},
      "type": "object",
    },
    "Record": {
      "additionalProperties": {
        "type": "string",
      },
      "properties": {},
      "type": "object",
    },
    "StringOrRegExp": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "type": "string",
        },
        {
          "format": "regex",
          "type": "string",
        },
      ],
    },
    "StringOrRegExp_2": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "type": "string",
        },
        {
          "format": "regex",
          "type": "string",
        },
      ],
    },
    "TopLevelFilterExpression": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "properties": {
            "expr": {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/FilterExpression",
            },
            "kind": {
              "const": "include",
              "type": "string",
            },
          },
          "required": [
            "kind",
            "expr",
          ],
          "type": "object",
        },
        {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "properties": {
            "expr": {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/FilterExpression",
            },
            "kind": {
              "const": "exclude",
              "type": "string",
            },
          },
          "required": [
            "kind",
            "expr",
          ],
          "type": "object",
        },
      ],
    },
  },
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "allOf": [
    {
      "properties": {
        "checks": {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "Controls which warnings are emitted during the build process. Each option can be set to \`true\` (emit warning) or \`false\` (suppress warning).",
          "properties": {
            "cannotCallNamespace": {
              "description": "Whether to emit warnings when a namespace is called as a function.

A module namespace object is an object and not a function. Calling it as a function will cause a runtime error.",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "circularDependency": {
              "description": "Whether to emit warnings when detecting circular dependency.

Circular dependencies lead to a bigger bundle size and sometimes cause execution order issues and are better to avoid.",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "commonJsVariableInEsm": {
              "description": "Whether to emit warnings when a CommonJS variable is used in an ES module.

CommonJS variables like \`module\` and \`exports\` are treated as global variables in ES modules and may not work as expected.",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "configurationFieldConflict": {
              "description": "Whether to emit warnings when a config value is overridden by another config value with a higher priority.",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "couldNotCleanDirectory": {
              "description": "Whether to emit warnings when Rolldown could not clean the output directory.

See [\`output.cleanDir\`](https://rolldown.rs/reference/OutputOptions.cleanDir).",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "duplicateShebang": {
              "description": "Whether to emit warnings when both the code and postBanner contain shebang

Having multiple shebangs in a file is a syntax error.",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "emptyImportMeta": {
              "description": "Whether to emit warnings when \`import.meta\` is not supported with the output format and is replaced with an empty object (\`{}\`).

See [\`import.meta\` in Non-ESM Output Formats page](https://rolldown.rs/in-depth/non-esm-output-formats#import-meta) for more details.",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "eval": {
              "description": "Whether to emit warnings when detecting uses of direct \`eval\`s.

See [Avoiding Direct \`eval\` in Troubleshooting page](https://rolldown.rs/guide/troubleshooting#avoiding-direct-eval) for more details.",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "filenameConflict": {
              "description": "Whether to emit warnings when files generated have the same name with different contents.",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "importIsUndefined": {
              "description": "Whether to emit warnings when an imported variable is not exported.

If the code is importing a variable that is not exported by the imported module, the value will always be \`undefined\`. This might be a mistake in the code.",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "ineffectiveDynamicImport": {
              "description": "Whether to emit warnings when a module is dynamically imported but also statically imported, making the dynamic import ineffective for code splitting.",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "invalidAnnotation": {
              "description": "Whether to emit warnings when a \`#__PURE__\` / \`@__PURE__\` annotation has no effect due to its position.

Annotations placed where they cannot annotate a call expression (e.g. before a non-call expression,
before a statement declaration, or between an identifier and \`=\` in a variable declarator) are
ignored by the parser. Matches Rollup's \`INVALID_ANNOTATION\` log code.

By default, warnings are emitted only for local project files inside \`cwd\` and outside
\`node_modules\`. Set this option to \`false\` to disable the warning entirely.",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "largeBarrelModules": {
              "description": "Whether to emit info logs when a barrel module has a very large number of re-exports (more than 5000).

Such modules can significantly slow down module resolution. Consider using
[\`@rolldown/plugin-transform-imports\`](https://github.com/rolldown/plugins/tree/main/packages/transform-imports)
to rewrite barrel imports at the source level so the barrel file is never loaded.

See [Large barrel modules](https://rolldown.rs/in-depth/lazy-barrel-optimization#large-barrel-modules) for more details.",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "missingGlobalName": {
              "description": "Whether to emit warnings when the \`output.globals\` option is missing when needed.

See [\`output.globals\`](https://rolldown.rs/reference/OutputOptions.globals).",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "missingNameOptionForIifeExport": {
              "description": "Whether to emit warnings when the \`output.name\` option is missing when needed.

See [\`output.name\`](https://rolldown.rs/reference/OutputOptions.name).",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "mixedExports": {
              "description": "Whether to emit warnings when the way to export values is ambiguous.

See [\`output.exports\`](https://rolldown.rs/reference/OutputOptions.exports).",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "pluginTimings": {
              "description": "Whether to emit warnings when plugins take significant time during the build process.",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "preferBuiltinFeature": {
              "description": "Whether to emit warnings when a plugin that is covered by a built-in feature is used.

Using built-in features is generally more performant than using plugins.",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "sourcemapBroken": {
              "description": "Whether to emit warnings when a plugin transforms code without generating a sourcemap.",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "toleratedTransform": {
              "description": "Whether to emit warnings when detecting tolerated transform.",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "unresolvedEntry": {
              "description": "Whether to emit warnings when an entrypoint cannot be resolved.",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "unresolvedImport": {
              "description": "Whether to emit warnings when an import cannot be resolved.",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "unsupportedTsconfigOption": {
              "description": "Whether to emit warnings when a tsconfig option or combination of options is not supported.",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
          },
          "type": "object",
        },
        "context": {
          "description": "The value of \`this\` at the top level of each module. **Normally, you don't need to set this option.**",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "cwd": {
          "description": "The working directory to use when resolving relative paths in the configuration.",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "devtools": {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "Devtools integration options.

When enabled, Rolldown writes JSON-lines devtools output under
\`node_modules/.rolldown/{session_id}/\`, resolved against {@linkcode cwd}.
Consumers can parse the output with \`@rolldown/debug\` after
\`await bundle.close()\` resolves.",
          "properties": {
            "sessionId": {
              "type": "string",
            },
          },
          "type": "object",
        },
        "experimental": {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "Experimental features that may change in future releases and can introduce behavior change without a major version bump.",
          "properties": {
            "attachDebugInfo": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "const": "none",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                {
                  "const": "simple",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                {
                  "const": "full",
                  "type": "string",
                },
              ],
              "description": "Attach debug information to the output bundle.

Available modes:
- \`none\`: No debug information is attached.
- \`simple\`: Attach comments indicating which files the bundled code comes from. These comments could be removed by the minifier.
- \`full\`: Attach detailed debug information to the output bundle. These comments are using legal comment syntax, so they won't be removed by the minifier.",
            },
            "chunkImportMap": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "const": false,
                  "type": "boolean",
                },
                {
                  "const": true,
                  "type": "boolean",
                },
                {
                  "additionalProperties": false,
                  "properties": {
                    "baseUrl": {
                      "type": "string",
                    },
                    "fileName": {
                      "type": "string",
                    },
                  },
                  "type": "object",
                },
              ],
              "description": "Enables automatic generation of a chunk import map asset during build.

This map only includes chunks with hashed filenames, where keys are derived from the facade module
name or primary chunk name. It produces stable and unique hash-based filenames, effectively preventing
cascading cache invalidation caused by content hashes and maximizing browser cache reuse.

The output defaults to \`importmap.json\` unless overridden via \`fileName\`. A base URL prefix
(default \`"/"\`) can be applied to all paths. The resulting JSON is a valid import map and can be
directly injected into HTML via \`<script type="importmap">\`.",
            },
            "chunkModulesOrder": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "const": "exec-order",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                {
                  "const": "module-id",
                  "type": "string",
                },
              ],
              "description": "Control which order should be used when rendering modules in a chunk.

Available options:
- \`exec-order\`: Almost equivalent to the topological order of the module graph, but specially handling when module graph has cycle.
- \`module-id\`: This is more friendly for gzip compression, especially for some javascript static asset lib (e.g. icon library)

> [!NOTE]
> Try to sort the modules by their module id if possible (Since rolldown scope hoist all modules in the chunk, we only try to sort those modules by module id if we could ensure runtime behavior is correct after sorting).",
            },
            "chunkOptimization": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "const": false,
                  "type": "boolean",
                },
                {
                  "const": true,
                  "type": "boolean",
                },
                {
                  "additionalProperties": false,
                  "properties": {
                    "avoidRedundantChunkLoads": {
                      "description": "Avoid emitting redundant chunk loads for dynamic entries.

This pass can reduce dynamic-entry dependent chunks when the shared modules
are guaranteed to be loaded by every importer of that dynamic entry.",
                      "type": "boolean",
                    },
                    "mergeCommonChunks": {
                      "description": "Merge common chunks into existing entry chunks when it is safe.

This can reduce the number of emitted chunks by moving shared/common modules
into an entry chunk that already depends on them. Rolldown only applies the
merge when it does not create a circular chunk dependency or change strict
entry export signatures. This pass also covers safe empty-facade cleanup.",
                      "type": "boolean",
                    },
                  },
                  "type": "object",
                },
              ],
              "description": "Control chunk optimizations.

\`true\` enables both common-chunk merging and redundant dynamic chunk-load avoidance.
\`false\` disables all chunk optimizations. Use the object form to control
\`mergeCommonChunks\` and \`avoidRedundantChunkLoads\` separately.

These optimizations are automatically disabled when any module uses top-level await (TLA) or contains TLA dependencies,
as they could affect execution order guarantees.",
            },
            "devMode": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "const": false,
                  "type": "boolean",
                },
                {
                  "const": true,
                  "type": "boolean",
                },
                {
                  "additionalProperties": false,
                  "properties": {
                    "host": {
                      "type": "string",
                    },
                    "implement": {
                      "type": "string",
                    },
                    "lazy": {
                      "type": "boolean",
                    },
                    "port": {
                      "type": "number",
                    },
                    "skipCommonRuntimeInjection": {
                      "deprecated": true,
                      "description": "Prevent Rolldown from prepending its common dev runtime to {@link implement }.",
                      "type": "boolean",
                    },
                  },
                  "type": "object",
                },
              ],
              "description": "Dev mode related options.",
            },
            "incrementalBuild": {
              "description": "Enable incremental build support. Required to be used with \`watch\` mode.",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "lazyBarrel": {
              "description": "Control whether to enable lazy barrel optimization.

Lazy barrel optimization avoids compiling unused re-export modules in side-effect-free barrel modules,
significantly improving build performance for large codebases with many barrel modules.

This option is planned to be removed in the future. If you need to opt out, please open an issue
describing your use case so we can address it before the option is gone.",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "nativeMagicString": {
              "description": "Use native Rust implementation of MagicString for source map generation.

[MagicString](https://github.com/rich-harris/magic-string) is a JavaScript library commonly used by bundlers
for string manipulation and source map generation. When enabled, rolldown will use a native Rust
implementation of MagicString instead of the JavaScript version, providing significantly better performance
during source map generation and code transformation.

**Benefits**

- **Improved Performance**: The native Rust implementation is typically faster than the JavaScript version,
  especially for large codebases with extensive source maps.
- **Background Processing**: Source map generation is performed asynchronously in a background thread,
  allowing the main bundling process to continue without blocking. This parallel processing can significantly
  reduce overall build times when working with JavaScript transform hooks.
- **Better Integration**: Seamless integration with rolldown's native Rust architecture.",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "onDemandWrapping": {
              "description": "Under \`output.strictExecutionOrder\`, derive a conservative wrapping plan from predicted
chunk execution hazards instead of wrapping every eligible module.",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "resolveNewUrlToAsset": {
              "description": "When enabled, \`new URL()\` calls will be transformed to a stable asset URL which includes the updated name and content hash.
It is necessary to pass \`import.meta.url\` as the second argument to the
\`new URL\` constructor, otherwise no transform will be applied.
:::warning
JavaScript and TypeScript files referenced via \`new URL('./file.js', import.meta.url)\` or \`new URL('./file.ts', import.meta.url)\` will **not** be transformed or bundled. The file will be copied as-is, meaning TypeScript files remain untransformed and dependencies are not resolved.

The expected behavior for JS/TS files is still being discussed and may
change in future releases. See [#7258](https://github.com/rolldown/rolldown/issues/7258) for more context.
:::",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "viteMode": {
              "description": "Enable Vite compatible mode.",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
          },
          "type": "object",
        },
        "external": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string",
            },
            {
              "format": "regex",
              "type": "string",
            },
            {
              "items": {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/StringOrRegExp",
              },
              "type": "array",
            },
            {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {},
              "type": "object",
            },
          ],
          "description": "Specifies which modules should be treated as external and not bundled. External modules will be left as import statements in the output.",
        },
        "input": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string",
            },
            {
              "items": {
                "type": "string",
              },
              "type": "array",
            },
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/Record",
            },
          ],
          "description": "Defines entries and location(s) of entry modules for the bundle. Relative paths are resolved based on the {@linkcode cwd} option.",
        },
        "logLevel": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "const": "info",
              "type": "string",
            },
            {
              "const": "debug",
              "type": "string",
            },
            {
              "const": "warn",
              "type": "string",
            },
            {
              "const": "silent",
              "type": "string",
            },
          ],
          "description": "Controls the verbosity of console logging during the build.",
        },
        "makeAbsoluteExternalsRelative": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "const": false,
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            {
              "const": true,
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            {
              "const": "ifRelativeSource",
              "type": "string",
            },
          ],
          "description": "Determines if absolute external paths should be converted to relative paths in the output.

This does not only apply to paths that are absolute in the source but also to paths that are resolved to an absolute path by either a plugin or Rolldown core.",
        },
        "moduleTypes": {
          "additionalProperties": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "const": "js",
                "type": "string",
              },
              {
                "const": "jsx",
                "type": "string",
              },
              {
                "const": "ts",
                "type": "string",
              },
              {
                "const": "tsx",
                "type": "string",
              },
              {
                "const": "json",
                "type": "string",
              },
              {
                "const": "text",
                "type": "string",
              },
              {
                "const": "base64",
                "type": "string",
              },
              {
                "const": "dataurl",
                "type": "string",
              },
              {
                "const": "binary",
                "type": "string",
              },
              {
                "const": "empty",
                "type": "string",
              },
              {
                "const": "css",
                "type": "string",
              },
              {
                "const": "asset",
                "type": "string",
              },
              {
                "const": "copy",
                "type": "string",
              },
            ],
          },
          "description": "Maps file patterns to module types, controlling how files are processed.

This is conceptually similar to [esbuild's \`loader\`](https://esbuild.github.io/api/#loader) option, allowing you to specify how each file extensions should be handled.

See [the In-Depth Guide](https://rolldown.rs/in-depth/module-types) for more details.",
          "properties": {},
          "type": "object",
        },
        "optimization": {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "Configure optimization features for the bundler.",
          "properties": {
            "inlineConst": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "const": false,
                  "type": "boolean",
                },
                {
                  "const": true,
                  "type": "boolean",
                },
                {
                  "additionalProperties": false,
                  "properties": {
                    "mode": {
                      "anyOf": [
                        {
                          "const": "all",
                          "type": "string",
                        },
                        {
                          "const": "smart",
                          "type": "string",
                        },
                      ],
                    },
                    "pass": {
                      "type": "number",
                    },
                  },
                  "type": "object",
                },
              ],
              "description": "Inline imported constant values during bundling instead of preserving variable references.

When enabled, constant values from imported modules will be inlined at their usage sites,
potentially reducing bundle size and improving runtime performance by eliminating variable lookups.

**Options:**
- \`true\`: equivalent to \`{ mode: 'all', pass: 1 }\`, enabling constant inlining for all eligible constants with a single pass.
- \`false\`: Disable constant inlining
- \`{ mode: 'smart' | 'all', pass?: number }\`:
  - \`mode: 'smart'\`: Only inline constants in specific scenarios where it is likely to reduce bundle size and improve performance.
    Smart mode inlines constants in these specific scenarios:
    1. \`if (test) {} else {}\` - condition expressions in if statements
    2. \`test ? a : b\` - condition expressions in ternary operators
    3. \`test1 || test2\` - logical OR expressions
    4. \`test1 && test2\` - logical AND expressions
    5. \`test1 ?? test2\` - nullish coalescing expressions
 - \`mode: 'all'\`: Inline all imported constants wherever they are used.
 - \`pass\`: Number of passes to perform for inlining constants.",
            },
            "pifeForModuleWrappers": {
              "description": "Use PIFE pattern for module wrappers.

Enabling this option improves the start up performance of the generated bundle with the cost of a slight increase in bundle size.",
              "type": "boolean",
            },
          },
          "type": "object",
        },
        "platform": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "const": "node",
              "type": "string",
            },
            {
              "const": "browser",
              "type": "string",
            },
            {
              "const": "neutral",
              "type": "string",
            },
          ],
          "description": "Expected platform where the code run.

 When the platform is set to neutral:
   - When bundling is enabled the default output format is set to esm, which uses the export syntax introduced with ECMAScript 2015 (i.e. ES6). You can change the output format if this default is not appropriate.
   - The main fields setting is empty by default. If you want to use npm-style packages, you will likely have to configure this to be something else such as main for the standard main field used by node.
   - The conditions setting does not automatically include any platform-specific values.",
        },
        "plugins": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "anyOf": [
