                      "type": "array",
                    },
                    "includeDependenciesRecursively": {
                      "description": "Global fallback of {@linkcode CodeSplittingGroup.includeDependenciesRecursivelygroup.includeDependenciesRecursively}, if it's not specified in the group.",
                      "type": "boolean",
                    },
                    "maxModuleSize": {
                      "description": "Global fallback of {@linkcode CodeSplittingGroup.maxModuleSizegroup.maxModuleSize}, if it's not specified in the group.",
                      "type": "number",
                    },
                    "maxSize": {
                      "description": "Global fallback of {@linkcode CodeSplittingGroup.maxSizegroup.maxSize}, if it's not specified in the group.",
                      "type": "number",
                    },
                    "minModuleSize": {
                      "description": "Global fallback of {@linkcode CodeSplittingGroup.minModuleSizegroup.minModuleSize}, if it's not specified in the group.",
                      "type": "number",
                    },
                    "minShareCount": {
                      "description": "Global fallback of {@linkcode CodeSplittingGroup.minShareCountgroup.minShareCount}, if it's not specified in the group.",
                      "type": "number",
                    },
                    "minSize": {
                      "description": "Global fallback of {@linkcode CodeSplittingGroup.minSizegroup.minSize}, if it's not specified in the group.",
                      "type": "number",
                    },
                  },
                  "type": "object",
                },
              ],
              "description": "Controls how code splitting is performed.

- \`true\`: Default behavior, automatic code splitting. **(default)**
- \`false\`: Inline all dynamic imports into a single bundle (equivalent to deprecated \`inlineDynamicImports: true\`).
- \`object\`: Advanced manual code splitting configuration.

For deeper understanding, please refer to the in-depth [documentation](https://rolldown.rs/in-depth/manual-code-splitting).",
            },
            "comments": {
              "anyOf": [
